  "test_scope": "H100 single GPU, fixed sparse routes, first gradients; no long-run convergence",
  "review": "# opt-r15 independent static review\n\nReviewer: subagent /root/projection_schedule. Implementers: /root, /root/backward_memory, /root/quant_activation. This record summarizes reviewer messages, not an independently executed GPU test.\n\nNative review found a blocker: no-C SM90 K-group TMA STORE flattens groups and M, so partial M tiles could overwrite the next expert. Implementation now rejects non-64-aligned M for nonempty multi-group overwrite and filters configurations where BLOCK_M does not divide M. Reviewer rechecked both guards, unchanged C-present/SM100/single-group/all-empty paths, the new 120-case regression design, and reported 27,088 legal output-store intervals with no cross-group write. No remaining confirmed blocker. Fresh GPU required.\n\nReviewer also checked the earlier multicast guard with a CPU schedule enumeration (6,830,208 physical pairs) and the gathered RHS packing/slice/scale strides. This is static formula validation, not GPU evidence.\n\nA separate scope review covered the new recompute module, main autograd 11-slot returns, MoE forwarding, BF16 rounding boundaries, unweighted zero-score router derivatives, bias2, saved-H immutability, empty paths and int64 addresses. Five reviewed files matched source-opt-r15. No confirmed blocker. Nonblocking recommendation: since both default and recompute now use the same dW1 column API, tighten their numerical test from 1% to byte equality; actual GPU records already report exactness separately.\n\nGPU results and source/install hashes are recorded separately by the opt-r15 runner.\n",
